      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T00:54:33Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post)!: the document's unit is the unit every post writes the program in\n\nThe document's Units choice (SetUnits, saved as `units`) is now the\nprogram's unit too - one setting, never the machine file's. The app\nstates it to every post as postOptions.Units (\"mm\" / \"inch\"); the\nengine refuses an inch document on a script whose manifest does not\ndeclare programUnits = \"mm inch\", by name, before any hook runs.\n\n- Fanuc, Haas, Mazak, Doosan DNM (G20) and Siemens 840D (G700) write\n  inch: lengths / 25.4 at four decimals, feeds in in/min at two; angles,\n  seconds and rpm unchanged. The three Tormach posts read the document\n  instead of machine.units.\n- Makera Carvera (mm-only firmware), Heidenhain and Fanuc Lathe refuse\n  an inch document by name (the latter two pending verified inch work).\n- PROJECT_VERSION 59: an older project opens on the unit its programs\n  posted in (from its machine files), with a load note when its display\n  changes, so it posts byte-identical.\n- Post section shows a \"Program units\" row (same SetUnits as the Stock\n  page); the post status line names the unit.\n- MCP: set_units tool; get_job reports units. post.exe: --units.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: a new document on an inch machine file (the shipped\nTormach machines) now posts mm until the document is set to inch;\nv59 project files are refused by older builds.\n\nFixes #902\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
