      "message": "fix(post): angle words never take the document unit; tinyg follows the unit law\n\nMain's angleWord (Fanuc, Doosan DNM, #997) wrote through `w`, which this\nchange made the unit-aware length word: an inch program would have\ndivided A/B/C by 25.4. It writes degrees through `wa` (resolved in the\nmerge). Pinned by program_units::rotary_angle_words_are_degrees_in_an_inch_program\n(RTCP arm and walk on the tilthead for both posts, Doosan's index path);\nwith `w` back in angleWord it fails (A1.4764 for A37.5).\n\ngrblHAL and TinyG (new on main) read machine.units: they now take the\nprogram unit from postOptions.Units and declare programUnits = \"mm inch\"\n(their inch path already scaled lengths and feeds). Pinned by\nprogram_units::grbl_family_posts_write_the_mm_program_in_inches and the\nupdated tinyg_post / grblhal_post inch tests.\n\nThe six inch drill_peck goldens re-recorded after #994 (G99 and the\nreturn move to R); no other golden moved.\n\nRefs #902\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
